### =====================================================================
### THE PAYOFF — the two endpoints that prove Campaign Memory works
### =====================================================================

### 47. Everything connected to one NPC in a single call:
###     who she is, who she knows, what she is involved in, what she carries.
###     This needs FOUR services, coordinated by NpcOrchestrator.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/npcs/2/detail
Accept: application/json

### 48. Memory counts for the campaign dashboard
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/1/memory/stats
Accept: application/json

### 49. ⭐ THE FULL SNAPSHOT — everything the app remembers about this campaign.
###     This exact payload is what the AI service will use as context in
###     Phase 3, so generated content always fits the existing world.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/1/memory
Accept: application/json


### =====================================================================
### PHASE 3 — THE CENTRAL AI SERVICE
###
### Pipeline:  1. collect context -> 2. build prompt -> 3. call model
###            -> 4. validate reply -> 5. store result
###
### Run 50-52 FIRST — they are completely free (no tokens spent).
### =====================================================================

### --- FREE: verify the setup without spending anything ---

### 50. Is the key loaded and which provider is active?
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/ai/status
Accept: application/json

### 51. ⭐ FREE + THE BEST PROOF THIS WORKS.
###     Shows the EXACT prompt that would be sent, without calling OpenAI.
###     Look at "userPrompt": it should contain Barovia, Castle Ravenloft,
###     the Cult of Strahd, Strahd, Ireena, Ismark, the active quests and
###     your party. That is Campaign Memory reaching the AI.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/1/ai/preview?type=NPC&instruction=A tavern keeper in the village
Accept: application/json

### 52. FREE: run the whole pipeline against the MOCK client.
###     "mock": true means no tokens are spent, but every step still runs.
###     Expect "mocked": true and a valid JSON "content" object.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/1/ai/generate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "NPC",
  "instruction": "A tavern keeper in the Village of Barovia.",
  "mock": true
}


### --- REAL GENERATION (these DO spend OpenAI tokens) ---

### 53. Generate an NPC that fits the existing world.
###     The reply should reference Barovia, the cult or the Kolyana family
###     WITHOUT you mentioning them — that is Campaign Memory at work.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/2/ai/generate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "NPC",
  "instruction": "A tavern keeper in the Village of Barovia who knows more than they admit."
}

### 54. Generate a quest. Note it should hook into existing NPCs.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/1/ai/generate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "QUEST",
  "instruction": "A side quest the party could take on while escorting Ireena."
}

### 55. Generate loot appropriate to the campaign's tone.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/1/ai/generate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "LOOT",
  "instruction": "Treasure found in a crypt beneath the village church.",
  "temperature": 0.9
}

### 56. Free-form question answered with full campaign context.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/1/ai/generate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "FREEFORM",
  "instruction": "What might Strahd do next, given what the party has done so far?"
}


### --- HISTORY AND USAGE ---

### 57. Everything generated for this campaign (newest first)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/1/ai/history
Accept: application/json

### 58. Token usage totals — the data Phase 5 will bill against
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/1/ai/usage
Accept: application/json

### 59. Preview the prompt for a different generation type.
###     Compare the output with #51: a LOOT request includes the known
###     items section, an NPC request includes the relationship web.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/1/ai/preview?type=LOOT&instruction=Treasure in a crypt
Accept: application/json


### =====================================================================
### PHASE 4 — THE CAMPAIGN GENERATOR (with the DM interview)
###
### The flow:
###   1. POST /interview  -> the AI asks YOU questions about your idea
###   2. you answer them
###   3. POST /generate   -> a full campaign is built AND SAVED as
###                          structured Campaign Memory, plus Session 1
###
### Requests 60-61 use "mock": true and are completely FREE.
### =====================================================================

### --- FREE: the whole flow against the mock client ---

### 60. STEP 1 (free): give a rough idea, get questions back.
###     Nothing is saved yet — this is just the interview.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/ai/campaign-generator/interview
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idea": "A campaign where the party slowly realises they are working for the villain.",
  "system": "D&D 5e",
  "tone": "dark, morally grey",
  "themes": "betrayal, loyalty, complicity",
  "playerCount": 4,
  "startingLevel": 3,
  "expectedLength": "about 12 sessions",
  "questionCount": 5,
  "mock": true
}

### 61. STEP 2 (free): generate the campaign from the idea + answers.
###     Expect 201 Created. Check the response "created" counts, then
###     look at the campaign in the database — the locations, factions,
###     NPCs and quests are all REAL ROWS, already linked to each other.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/ai/campaign-generator/generate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idea": "A campaign where the party slowly realises they are working for the villain.",
  "system": "D&D 5e",
  "tone": "dark, morally grey",
  "themes": "betrayal, loyalty, complicity",
  "playerCount": 4,
  "startingLevel": 3,
  "answers": [
    {
      "questionId": "central_conflict",
      "question": "What is the central conflict driving this campaign?",
      "answer": "A benevolent-seeming order is quietly harvesting a city's memories."
    },
    {
      "questionId": "villain_goal",
      "question": "What does the villain actually want?",
      "answer": "To erase a historical atrocity from every living mind, including their own."
    },
    {
      "questionId": "party_stake",
      "question": "Why is this party the one that has to deal with it?",
      "answer": "They are the order's most trusted field agents."
    }
  ],
  "additionalNotes": "I want at least one NPC the party will feel terrible about betraying.",
  "locationCount": 5,
  "factionCount": 3,
  "npcCount": 6,
  "questCount": 4,
  "mock": true
}

### 62. Confirm it was really saved. Use the campaign id returned by #61.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/2/memory/stats
Accept: application/json

### 63. The generated world, fully connected (NPCs linked to locations/factions,
###     quests linked to givers and NPCs).
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/2/memory
Accept: application/json

### 64. The generated Session 1 plan, stored as a real session.
###     Its "notes" contain the opening scene, beats, encounters and cliffhanger.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/campaigns/2/sessions
Accept: application/json


### --- REAL GENERATION (these DO spend OpenAI tokens) ---

### 65. STEP 1 for real: the AI interviews you about your idea.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/ai/campaign-generator/interview
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idea": "A seafaring campaign where every island remembers a different version of history.",
  "system": "D&D 5e",
  "tone": "wondrous but unsettling",
  "themes": "memory, truth, colonialism",
  "playerCount": 5,
  "startingLevel": 1,
  "expectedLength": "long campaign, 1 to 12",
  "questionCount": 6
}

### 66. STEP 2 for real: paste YOUR answers from #65 below, then run this.
###     The generated campaign should visibly honour every answer you gave.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/ai/campaign-generator/generate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idea": "A seafaring campaign where every island remembers a different version of history.",
  "system": "D&D 5e",
  "tone": "wondrous but unsettling",
  "themes": "memory, truth, colonialism",
  "playerCount": 5,
  "startingLevel": 1,
  "expectedLength": "long campaign, 1 to 12",
  "answers": [
    {
      "questionId": "replace_me",
      "question": "paste a question from the interview response",
      "answer": "your answer"
    }
  ],
  "additionalNotes": "",
  "locationCount": 6,
  "factionCount": 3,
  "npcCount": 8,
  "questCount": 5,
  "temperature": 0.9
}

### 67. Generating without doing the interview also works — the answers
###     array is simply optional.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/ai/campaign-generator/generate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idea": "A heist campaign set in a city where magic is illegal.",
  "system": "D&D 5e",
  "tone": "sharp, stylish",
  "locationCount": 4,
  "factionCount": 3,
  "npcCount": 5,
  "questCount": 3
}




